1
00:00:00,512 --> 00:00:04,252
(chuckles):
Get a load of this guy.

2
00:00:04,249 --> 00:00:06,619
(Howard:)Can you imagine if we
make money with this?

3
00:00:06,618 --> 00:00:08,188
(Leonard:)If we do,
I am splurging

4
00:00:08,186 --> 00:00:10,926
(Leonard:)on the best sinus irrigator
money can buy.

5
00:00:12,457 --> 00:00:13,627
(Howard:)That old sad story...

6
00:00:13,625 --> 00:00:16,665
(Howard:)guy gets a little money,
goes straight up his nose.

7
00:00:16,662 --> 00:00:20,402
(Attorney:)Just need you to review
and sign this document

8
00:00:20,399 --> 00:00:22,529
(Attorney:)acknowledging that you
understand the university

9
00:00:22,534 --> 00:00:25,404
(Attorney:)will own 75% of the patent.

10
00:00:26,505 --> 00:00:28,775
75%?

11
00:00:28,774 --> 00:00:29,904
(Sheldon:)That's outrageous.

12
00:00:29,908 --> 00:00:32,708
(Sheldon:)This is our idea
based on our research.

13
00:00:32,711 --> 00:00:35,881
(Sheldon:)How can you possibly justify
owning a majority share?

14
00:00:35,881 --> 00:00:37,351
(Attorney:)It's university policy.

15
00:00:37,349 --> 00:00:39,619
(Sheldon:)I know when I'm beat.

16
00:00:39,618 --> 00:00:41,988
(Leonard:)Hold on, hold on.
So the three of us

17
00:00:41,987 --> 00:00:45,487
(Leonard:)do all the work
and only end up with 25%?

18
00:00:45,490 --> 00:00:47,460
(Attorney:)Dr. Hofstadter, this university

19
00:00:47,459 --> 00:00:49,389
(Attorney:)has been paying your salaries
for over ten years.

20
00:00:49,394 --> 00:00:52,094
(Attorney:)Did you think we do that out
of the goodness of our hearts?

21
00:00:52,097 --> 00:00:55,897
(Leonard:)Well, until you just said
that mean thing, kinda.

22
00:00:57,035 --> 00:00:59,065
(Attorney:)And as far as
Mr. Wolowitz is concerned,

23
00:00:59,071 --> 00:01:02,301
(Attorney:)I'm afraid as a federal employee
on loan from NASA,

24
00:01:02,307 --> 00:01:04,077
(Attorney:)your name can be
on the patent,

25
00:01:04,076 --> 00:01:07,476
(Attorney:)but you're not entitled
to an ownership share.

26
00:01:07,479 --> 00:01:09,749
(Howard:)Wait, so this can turn out to be

27
00:01:09,748 --> 00:01:12,918
(Howard:)a financial success,
and I get nothing?

28
00:01:12,918 --> 00:01:16,818
(Attorney:)Well, sometimes
they give you a plaque.

29
00:01:16,822 --> 00:01:18,322
(Sheldon:)Well, that's not fair.

30
00:01:18,323 --> 00:01:20,393
(Sheldon:)We should all get plaques.

31
00:01:22,861 --> 00:01:24,531
(Leonard:)Sorry, but we
can't sign this.

32
00:01:24,529 --> 00:01:26,199
(Howard:)Come on, let's go.

33
00:01:26,198 --> 00:01:28,128
(Leonard:)Thank you for your time.

34
00:01:30,869 --> 00:01:33,299
(Sheldon:)Couple of questions
about the plaque...

35
00:01:34,373 --> 00:01:37,973
♪ Our whole universe
was in a hot, dense state ♪

